IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-art2-entity`
IMPORT `g1-art2-governor-misconduct`
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g4-nouns`
IMPORT `g4-art11-decision`
IMPORT `g4-art12-name`
IMPORT `g5-nouns`
IMPORT `g5-art14-court-powers`
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-art15-16-deregistration`
IMPORT `g6-art17-after-deregistration`
IMPORT `g6-art18-governor-duties`
IMPORT `g6-art19-reportable-matters`
IMPORT `g6-art20-court-orders`
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-vintages`
IMPORT `g7-art21-23-expressions`
IMPORT `g8-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-art27-28-required-steps`
IMPORT `g9-sched1-commissioner`
IMPORT `int-readings`
IMPORT `int-nouns`
IMPORT `int-commencement`
IMPORT `int-vintage`
IMPORT `int-wiring`
IMPORT `int-h-register`

-- int-h-contravention.l4: headline (c) of the integration layer: what follows from a contravention of the Law, or from a reportable matter?
-- A contravention is a fact about a registered charity or one of its governors. What follows is decided by four groups and joined here (PLAN section 10, item 5):
--   * whether the charity's conduct is "misconduct" (Article 2(10), group G1, IP12) needs "a provision of this Law has been contravened" (IP13), which no group decides alone: each duty or prohibition
--     decides its own breach. The integration layer maps the breaches that groups G4 and G6 decide as Booleans (the name, Articles 19(2), 19(4), 19(10), 20(6)); a breach that a group records only as a DEONTIC
--     rule's BREACH (Articles 13(4), 13(5), 13(11)(a), 18, 19(8)) enters as the input "a duty or prohibition was breached, as a trace of the rule shows";
--   * whether a governor "engages in misconduct" (Article 18(4), group G6, IP14) reads the charity's misconduct and the other governors' conduct;
--   * the Commissioner's powers: a required steps notice (Article 27, group G8), deregistration (Article 16, group G6), an application to the court (Article 14, group G5; IP28: someone is acting as
--     the Commissioner, group G9); the governors' duties (Article 19, group G6); and what follows a deregistration (Article 17, group G6).
-- It rests on Articles 2, 5, 12, 14, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 22, 27 and refuses for a day before Part 4 or Part 5 (1 May 2018) was in force, and for a day on which the text changed and the two texts answer differently.

§ `Integration layer -- headline (c): what follows from a contravention or a reportable matter?`

-- generated by gen_replace.py: a copy of `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` (module g6-art18-governor-duties) with the field `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)` replaced
GIVEN original IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` @desc The record to copy
      replacement IS A BOOLEAN @desc The new value of the field `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)`
GIVETH A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
`Int the conduct of a governor with the misconduct finding` original replacement MEANS
    `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` WITH
        `name` IS original's `name`
        `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS replacement
        `concurs in the misconduct of the charity` IS original's `concurs in the misconduct of the charity`
        `assists or encourages these other governors to engage in misconduct` IS original's `assists or encourages these other governors to engage in misconduct`
        `becomes aware or ought to have become aware of misconduct, or of the intention of another governor to engage in it` IS original's `becomes aware or ought to have become aware of misconduct, or of the intention of another governor to engage in it`
        `actively conceals that misconduct or that intention` IS original's `actively conceals that misconduct or that intention`
        `continues the concealment beyond a reasonable time` IS original's `continues the concealment beyond a reasonable time`
        `fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps to protect or restore the property of the charity or to prevent the misconduct` IS original's `fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps to protect or restore the property of the charity or to prevent the misconduct`


-- A contravention of the Law, as it enters the question.
DECLARE `Contravention of this Law in the case` IS ONE OF
    `a name other than a registered or related name was used`
        HAS used IS A `Name used by a registered charity` @desc The name used and its relation to the charity's registered names (Article 12(7))
    `a governor is in breach of the duty to report`
        HAS governor IS A Governor @desc The governor
            `longest interval that counts as prompt, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The interval an input judgement fixes as prompt (fork F6.12), if it does
            position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` @desc When the matter arose and was reported (Article 19(2))
    `a governor is in breach of the duty to give a declaration`
        HAS governor IS A Governor @desc The governor
            position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(4)` @desc When the charity notified the governor and when the declaration was given (Article 19(4))
    `a person acted as a governor after reporting a reportable matter`
        HAS position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` @desc When the matter was reported (Article 19(10))
            permissions IS A LIST OF `Permission to act as a governor` @desc The permissions to act as a governor given to the person
            `the act is done in accordance with any condition on the permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act is within any condition on the permission
    `a person contravened a disqualification order`
        HAS order IS A `Disqualification order` @desc The disqualification order
            person IS A STRING @desc The person
            `the person is a governor of, or concerned or takes part in the management of, a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is, or takes part in the management of, a registered charity
            `the court has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has given leave
    `a duty or prohibition was breached, as a trace of the rule shows`
        HAS rule IS A STRING @desc The rule whose #TRACE ends in BREACH, for example Article 19(8) or Article 13(11)(a)

-- IP13: whether ONE contravention is a contravention of a provision of this Law, decided by the group that decides the provision.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      charity IS A `Registered charity` @desc The charity (IP7), read by Article 12(7)
      registered IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP6: whether the entity is a registered charity
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      contravention IS A `Contravention of this Law in the case` @desc The contravention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP13 the contravention is a contravention of this Law` readings charity registered day contravention MEANS
    CONSIDER contravention
      WHEN `a name other than a registered or related name was used` used THEN NOT `Art 12(7) the name used is permitted` (readings's `reading of Articles 11 and 12`) charity used
      WHEN `a governor is in breach of the duty to report` governor interval position THEN `Art 19(2) the governor is in breach of paragraph (2)` (readings's `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) interval day governor position
      WHEN `a governor is in breach of the duty to give a declaration` governor position THEN `Art 19(4) the governor is in breach of paragraph (4)` (readings's `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) registered day governor position
      WHEN `a person acted as a governor after reporting a reportable matter` position permissions accordance THEN `Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (readings's `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) registered position permissions day accordance
      WHEN `a person contravened a disqualification order` order person inRegistered leave THEN `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` order person day inRegistered leave
      WHEN `a duty or prohibition was breached, as a trace of the rule shows` rule THEN TRUE

GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      charity IS A `Registered charity` @desc The charity (IP7)
      registered IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP6
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      contraventions IS A LIST OF `Contravention of this Law in the case` @desc The contraventions alleged
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP13 a provision of this Law has been contravened` readings charity registered day contraventions MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD `Int IP13 the contravention is a contravention of this Law` readings charity registered day c) contraventions

-- One governor's conduct, as Article 18(4) reads it: group G6's record with its Article 2(10) finding filled in by group G1 (IP12) from the governor's own conduct facts.
DECLARE `Governor conduct in the case` HAS
    conduct IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` @desc The governor's conduct as Article 18(4) reads it; its field on Article 2(10) is filled in from `own conduct facts`
    `own conduct facts` IS A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)` @desc The facts that decide whether the governor's own conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)
    `own contraventions` IS A LIST OF `Contravention of this Law in the case` @desc The contraventions of this Law by the governor himself or herself

-- generated by gen_replace.py: a copy of `Deregistration of the entity` (module g6-art17-after-deregistration) with the field `date of the deregistration` replaced
GIVEN original IS A `Deregistration of the entity` @desc The record to copy
      replacement IS A DATE @desc The new value of the field `date of the deregistration`
GIVETH A `Deregistration of the entity`
`Int the deregistration with the date it was served` original replacement MEANS
    `Deregistration of the entity` WITH
        `route` IS original's `route`
        `date of the deregistration` IS replacement
        `date of the preliminary notice` IS original's `date of the preliminary notice`
        `the Commissioner is satisfied that the grounds have existed since` IS original's `the Commissioner is satisfied that the grounds have existed since`
        `past date specified in the deregistration notice` IS original's `past date specified in the deregistration notice`
        `past date specified in the preliminary notice` IS original's `past date specified in the preliminary notice`
        `the Commissioner determines that the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` IS original's `the Commissioner determines that the deregistration takes effect retrospectively`


-- The deregistration, with the notice by which it was made: its date is the date on which that notice was served, fixed by group G7 (Article 38, IP34), not an input.
DECLARE `Deregistration in the case` HAS
    deregistration IS A `Deregistration of the entity` @desc The route and the dates group G6 reads; its field `date of the deregistration` is replaced by the date on which the notice was served
    notice IS A `Notice of a decision in the case` @desc The deregistration notice, with the dates that fix its service under Article 38

-- The case.
DECLARE `Contravention case` HAS
    charity IS A `Register entry in the case` @desc The registered charity, what the register records about it and its people
    contraventions IS A LIST OF `Contravention of this Law in the case` @desc The contraventions of this Law alleged against the charity
    conduct IS A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)` @desc The facts that decide whether the charity's conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)
    `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` @desc Group G7's facts for Article 22 (read for Article 2(10)(b))
    `conduct of the governors` IS A LIST OF `Governor conduct in the case` @desc One entry per governor whose conduct Article 18(4) reads
    `the Commissioner's beliefs` IS A LIST OF `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc The beliefs among the five of Article 27(1) that the Commissioner holds
    `a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The determination of Article 27(1)(d)
    `facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)` IS A `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)` @desc The facts about the grounds of Article 16(1) and the Commissioner's satisfaction
    `preliminary notice` IS A MAYBE `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)` @desc The preliminary notice of Article 16(1); NOTHING if none has been given
    deregistration IS A MAYBE `Deregistration in the case` @desc The deregistration, if the Commissioner has deregistered the entity
    `application to the court` IS A `Application to the court under Article 14` @desc The application to the court (Article 14)
    `what appears to the court` IS A `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` @desc What appears to the court (Article 14(1))
    `the charity carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 11(4)(c)(ii), read for Article 27(1)(e): the charity's activity in Jersey
    `the activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 11(4)(c)(ii): the Commissioner's opinion that the activity is substantial
    `a relevant person has been designated under sub-paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has designated a relevant person (Schedule 1 paragraph 4(4))
    `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person appointed is unable to act through incapacity or absence (Schedule 1 paragraph 4(5))
    `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a vacancy (Schedule 1 paragraph 4(5))

DECLARE `Reportable matters of a governor` HAS
    name IS A STRING @desc The governor
    matters IS A LIST OF `Kind of reportable matter` @desc The kinds of reportable matter that describe the governor (Article 19(1), IP21)

DECLARE `Effects of a deregistration` HAS
    `the basis of the deregistration` IS A `Basis of deregistration` @desc IP32, group G6: Article 16 or 15
    `date deregistered` IS A DATE @desc Group G6: Article 17(3): the date from which the termination takes effect (retrospective or not)
    `the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Group G6: Article 17(2)
    `last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` IS A DATE @desc Group G6: Article 17(1)(a)

DECLARE `Consequences of a contravention` HAS
    `a provision of this Law has been contravened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP13, from the groups that decide each provision
    `the charity's conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP12, group G1
    `the governors who engage in misconduct within Article 18(4)` IS A LIST OF STRING @desc IP14, group G6: the names
    `the reportable matters of each governor` IS A LIST OF `Reportable matters of a governor` @desc IP21, group G6: Article 19(1)
    `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP8, group G2
    `the grounds on which the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice` IS A LIST OF `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc Group G8: Article 27(1)
    `a ground of Article 16(1) for deregistration exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Group G6: Article 16(1)(a) to (d)
    `the powers of the court under Article 14 are exercisable on the Commissioner's application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Group G5: Article 14(1)
    `someone is acting as the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP28, group G9: Schedule 1 paragraph 4(5)
    `the effects of the deregistration` IS A MAYBE `Effects of a deregistration` @desc Group G6: Article 17, if the entity has been deregistered


-- One governor's conduct for Article 18(4), with the finding on Article 2(10) made by group G1 (IP12) from the governor's own conduct facts and own contraventions (IP13).
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      notices IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice` @desc IP19
      excepted IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP26
      registered IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP6
      charity IS A `Registered charity` @desc IP7
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      gc IS A `Governor conduct in the case` @desc The governor's conduct
GIVETH A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
`Int the governor conduct with the finding` readings notices excepted registered charity day gc MEANS
    `Int the conduct of a governor with the misconduct finding` (gc's conduct)
        (`Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` (readings's `reading of Articles 1 and 2`) (gc's `own conduct facts`) excepted (`Int IP13 a provision of this Law has been contravened` readings charity registered day (gc's `own contraventions`)) notices)

-- The consequences under ONE text of the Law.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law
      case IS A `Contravention case` @desc The case
GIVETH A `Consequences of a contravention`
`Int (c) the consequences of the contravention under the text` readings day vintage case MEANS
    `Consequences of a contravention` WITH
        `a provision of this Law has been contravened` IS contravened
        `the charity's conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS misconduct
        `the governors who engage in misconduct within Article 18(4)` IS map (GIVEN c YIELD c's name) (filter (GIVEN c YIELD `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` g6 misconduct governorConducts c) governorConducts)
        `the reportable matters of each governor` IS map (GIVEN g YIELD `Reportable matters of a governor` OF (g's name), (g's `reportable matters`)) (entity's governors)
        `the entity meets the charity test` IS charityTest
        `the grounds on which the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice` IS `Art 27(1) the Commissioner has a ground to serve a required steps notice` (readings's `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) isRegistered (case's `the Commissioner's beliefs`) misconduct charityTest anyGovernorMisconduct entity (case's `a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter`) ip15 ip16
        `a ground of Article 16(1) for deregistration exists` IS `Art 16(1) a ground of Article 16(1) exists` g6 charityTest notices (case's `facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)`) day
        `the powers of the court under Article 14 are exercisable on the Commissioner's application` IS acting AND `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` (readings's `reading of Articles 13 and 14`) isRegistered `an application by the Commissioner` misconduct (case's `what appears to the court`)
        `someone is acting as the Commissioner` IS acting
        `the effects of the deregistration` IS
            CONSIDER case's deregistration
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
              WHEN JUST inCase THEN JUST (`Effects of a deregistration` WITH
                    `the basis of the deregistration` IS `Art 16 the basis of deregistration` ((inCase's deregistration)'s route)
                    `date deregistered` IS `Art 17(3) the date deregistered` g6 (dereg inCase)
                    `the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` IS `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` g6 (dereg inCase)
                    `last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` IS `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` g6 (dereg inCase))
    WHERE
        g6 MEANS readings's `reading of Articles 15 to 20`
        dereg MEANS GIVEN d YIELD `Int the deregistration with the date it was served` (d's deregistration) (`Int IP34 the date on which the notice of a decision was served` readings (d's notice))
        register MEANS case's charity
        notices MEANS `Int IP19 the required steps notices served` readings (register's `notices served`)
        entity MEANS `Int IP5 the entity` readings vintage notices day (register's body)
        isRegistered MEANS `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` entity
        charityRecord MEANS `Int IP7 the registered charity` readings entity register
        contravened MEANS `Int IP13 a provision of this Law has been contravened` readings charityRecord isRegistered day (case's contraventions)
        excepted MEANS `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` (case's `facts for the excepted foreign charity test`) isRegistered
        misconduct MEANS `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` (readings's `reading of Articles 1 and 2`) (case's conduct) excepted contravened notices
        charityTest MEANS `Int IP8 the entity meets the charity test` readings vintage entity ((register's body)'s purposes) (register's `charity test facts`)
        governorConducts MEANS map (GIVEN gc YIELD `Int the governor conduct with the finding` readings notices excepted isRegistered charityRecord day gc) (case's `conduct of the governors`)
        anyGovernorMisconduct MEANS any (GIVEN c YIELD `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` g6 misconduct governorConducts c) governorConducts
        ip15 MEANS `Art 11(4)(c) the requirement is met` entity (case's `the charity carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey`) (case's `the activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial`)
        ip16 MEANS `Art 11(4)(d) the requirement is met` (`Int IP17 the entity has a principal address in Jersey` readings entity (register's `facts for the principal address`))
        acting MEANS `Sch 1 para 4(5) someone is treated as the Commissioner` (case's `a relevant person has been designated under sub-paragraph (4)`) (case's `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act`) (case's `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner`)

-- The Articles the question rests on, as now numbered. Article 22 is read for Article 2(10)(b) (trap T30: Part 5 came into force a year and a half before Article 22).
`Int (c) the units the question rests on` MEANS
    LIST `Int Article` 2, `Int Article` 5, `Int Article` 12, `Int Article` 14, `Int Article` 16, `Int Article` 17, `Int Article` 18, `Int Article` 19, `Int Article` 20, `Int Article` 22, `Int Article` 27

@export What follows from a contravention of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 by a registered charity or one of its governors, or from a reportable matter: whether the charity's conduct is misconduct (Article 2(10)), which governors engage in misconduct (Article 18(4)), which kinds of reportable matter describe each governor (Article 19(1)), the grounds on which the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice (Article 27(1)), whether a ground of deregistration exists (Article 16(1)), whether the court's powers are exercisable on the Commissioner's application (Article 14(1)), whether someone is acting as the Commissioner (Schedule 1 paragraph 4(5)), and, if the entity has been deregistered, the effects of the deregistration (Article 17). Refuses for a day before Parts 4 and 5 were in force or Article 22 was in force (1 January 2019), and for a day on which the text changed and the two texts answer differently
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups (the favoured readings are `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`)
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked, for example 2026-10-02 (ISO 8601)
      case IS A `Contravention case` @desc The registered charity, the contraventions alleged, the facts about its conduct and its governors' conduct, the Commissioner's beliefs and the facts the powers read
GIVETH A `Consequences of a contravention`
`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` readings day case MEANS
    `Int the answer if every unit is in force` `Int (c) the units the question rests on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        (`Int the answer under every text of the Law in force on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
            (GIVEN vintage YIELD `Int (c) the consequences of the contravention under the text` readings day vintage case))

-- The proposed required steps notice: the belief relied on and the facts Article 27(2) and (3) read.
DECLARE `Notice proposed in the case` HAS
    belief IS A `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc The belief of Article 27(1) the notice rests on
    `the person is a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person served is the registered charity or one of its governors (Article 27(3))
    `the notice specifies the steps and a time for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice specifies the steps and a time (Article 27(2))
    `the steps are in the Commissioner's opinion appropriate to remedy the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Commissioner's opinion (Article 27(2))
    `the procedure and restrictions of any Order under Article 27(5) are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the procedure and restrictions of any Order under Article 27(5) are met

-- The Commissioner's power to serve a required steps notice: open when one of the beliefs of Article 27(1) is a ground, as the facts of the case make it.
@export The Commissioner's power under Article 27(2) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 to serve a required steps notice on the registered charity or one of its governors, as a regulative rule: available when a belief of Article 27(1) is a ground on the facts of the case. Refuses as the other headline functions do
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
      case IS A `Contravention case` @desc The case
      notice IS A `Notice proposed in the case` @desc The notice the Commissioner proposes to serve
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 26 to 31`
`Int (c) the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice` readings day case notice MEANS
    `Int the answer if every unit is in force` `Int (c) the units the question rests on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        (`Art 27(2) the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice`
            ((`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` readings day case)'s `the grounds on which the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice`)
            (notice's belief) (notice's `the person is a relevant person`) (notice's `the notice specifies the steps and a time for them`)
            (notice's `the steps are in the Commissioner's opinion appropriate to remedy the matter`) (notice's `the procedure and restrictions of any Order under Article 27(5) are met`))

-- The Commissioner's power to deregister under Article 16(1).
@export The Commissioner's power under Article 16(1) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 to deregister a registered charity by written notice, as a regulative rule: open when a ground exists, a preliminary notice giving reasons and inviting objections has been given and has run its time, and the Commissioner is satisfied that deregistering is proportionate. Refuses for a day on which the text of the Law changed
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Commissioner would deregister
      case IS A `Contravention case` @desc The case
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`Int (c) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` readings day case MEANS
    `Int the answer if every unit is in force` `Int (c) the units the question rests on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        (`Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` (readings's `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) isRegistered charityTest notices (case's `facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)`) (case's `preliminary notice`) day)
    WHERE
        vintage MEANS `Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        notices MEANS `Int IP19 the required steps notices served` readings ((case's charity)'s `notices served`)
        entity MEANS `Int IP5 the entity` readings vintage notices day ((case's charity)'s body)
        isRegistered MEANS `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` entity
        charityTest MEANS `Int IP8 the entity meets the charity test` readings vintage entity (((case's charity)'s body)'s purposes) ((case's charity)'s `charity test facts`)

-- The court's power under Article 14(1), on the Commissioner's application.
@export The court's power under Article 14(1) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 to exercise its powers over a registered charity on the Commissioner's application, as a regulative rule: open when someone is acting as the Commissioner (Schedule 1 paragraph 4(5)) and the charity's conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10) or the court is satisfied as Article 14(1) requires. Refuses for a day on which the text of the Law changed
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the application is made
      case IS A `Contravention case` @desc The case
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 14`
`Int (c) the court may exercise its powers on the Commissioner's application` readings day case MEANS
    `Int the answer if every unit is in force` `Int (c) the units the question rests on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        (`Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` (readings's `reading of Articles 13 and 14`) isRegistered acting `an application by the Commissioner` misconduct (case's `what appears to the court`))
    WHERE
        vintage MEANS `Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        consequences MEANS `Int (c) the consequences of the contravention under the text` readings day vintage case
        notices MEANS `Int IP19 the required steps notices served` readings ((case's charity)'s `notices served`)
        entity MEANS `Int IP5 the entity` readings vintage notices day ((case's charity)'s body)
        isRegistered MEANS `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` entity
        misconduct MEANS consequences's `the charity's conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)`
        acting MEANS consequences's `someone is acting as the Commissioner`

-- The governor of the entity with a given name, with the reportable matters found by group G6 (IP21).
GIVEN entity IS AN Entity @desc The entity, whose governors carry the reportable matters found
      name IS A STRING @desc The name asked about
GIVETH A Governor
`Int the governor named` entity name MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN g YIELD g's name EQUALS name) (entity's governors)
      WHEN EMPTY THEN REFUSE "the name given is not that of a governor of the entity on the day asked about"
      WHEN g FOLLOWED BY rest THEN g

-- The governor's duty to report a reportable matter (Article 19(2)): it binds a governor of a registered charity.
-- The governor is named, not supplied: the reportable matters that make the duty bind are found by group G6 from the person's own facts in the case (IP21), so a caller cannot hand in a governor whose matters were left empty.
-- (An earlier version took a Governor record. Its traces passed vacuously, because the record built by hand had no reportable matters and the duty then does not bind; check-traces.py caught it.)
@export The duty of a governor of a registered charity under Article 19(2) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 to report any reportable matter promptly to the charity and to the Commissioner, as a regulative rule. Refuses for a day on which the text of the Law changed
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
      case IS A `Contravention case` @desc The case
      name IS A STRING @desc The name of the governor, as entered for the person in the case (a person who is not a governor of the entity on the day asked about is a refusal, not a duty that does not bind)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 19`
`Int (c) the governor must report the reportable matter` readings day case name MEANS
    `Int the answer if every unit is in force` `Int (c) the units the question rests on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        (`Art 19(2) the governor must report the reportable matter` isRegistered entity (`Int the governor named` entity name))
    WHERE
        vintage MEANS `Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        notices MEANS `Int IP19 the required steps notices served` readings ((case's charity)'s `notices served`)
        entity MEANS `Int IP5 the entity` readings vintage notices day ((case's charity)'s body)
        isRegistered MEANS `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` entity
